{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Download one folder of runtime/files/shared as a zip archive (File return type). The path is share-relative and validated by resolve_path; empty means the whole share. A named folder is archived as one top-level folder, the share root as its contents. Runs the system `zip` (argv, no shell; -y stores symlinks as links, never follows them) into runtime/files/zips, a scratch directory outside the share whose archives older than one hour are swept on each call. Errors: 403 invalid path, 404 missing, 405 not a folder, 500 zip missing or failed. Open to admin and the files group, so a peer reaches it at /peer/remote/<uuid>/files/zip_dir.","groups":"files","import":"use std::path::Path;\nuse std::time::{Duration, SystemTime, UNIX_EPOCH};\nuse crate::files::files::resolve_path::resolve_path;","params":[{"desc":"Share-relative folder below runtime/files/shared; empty means the whole share.","name":"path","type":"String"}],"returntype":"File","type":"rust"},"id":"mwnzrp1a1c8956395o1","readers":["files"],"time":1794366604418,"username":"system","writers":[]}